      "message": "how to build native_shared_libs depends on the compile_multilib value, if it is \"both\" native_shared_libs should be built for both, for example, I have these in the bp file:\n    compile_multilib: \"both\",\n    multilib: {\n        both: {\n            native_shared_libs: [\n                \"libadb_pairing_connection\",\n                \"libadb_pairing_server\",\n                \"libadbconnection_client\",\n            ],\n        },\n    },\n    native_shared_libs: [\n        \"libadb_pairing_auth\",\n    ],\n\nand soong build gives me these:\n\nyudiliu@yudiliu:~/android/aosp/master$ ls -l out/target/product/vsoc_arm64/system/apex/com.android.adbd.capex \n-rw-r--r-- 1 yudiliu primarygroup 4177920 Oct 10 11:57 out/target/product/vsoc_arm64/system/apex/com.android.adbd.capex\nyudiliu@yudiliu:~/android/aosp/master$ deapexer list out/target/product/vsoc_arm64/system/apex/com.android.adbd.capex\n./apex_manifest.pb\n./bin/adbd\n./etc/init.rc\n./lib/libadb_pairing_auth.so\n./lib/libadb_pairing_connection.so\n./lib/libadb_pairing_server.so\n./lib/libadbconnection_client.so\n./lib/libbase.so\n./lib/libc++.so\n./lib/libcrypto.so\n./lib/libcrypto_utils.so\n./lib/libcutils.so\n./lib64/libadb_pairing_auth.so\n./lib64/libadb_pairing_connection.so\n./lib64/libadb_pairing_server.so\n./lib64/libadbconnection_client.so\n./lib64/libbase.so\n./lib64/libc++.so\n./lib64/libcrypto.so\n./lib64/libcrypto_utils.so\n./lib64/libcutils.so\nyudiliu@yudiliu:~/android/aosp/master$",
